# The DeepFellow Dashboard artifact lives in the Modular Frontend project's own GitLab package registry while the
# product is not ready to be public. Both lines move together on the day it goes to the public registry: an npm
# authentication line is keyed to the host AND the path, so a registry change alone leaves a line matching nothing.
# package-lock.json records the download URL too, so it has to be regenerated in the same change.
#
# GITLAB_NPM_TOKEN is a name each context fills for itself, and it is stored in no file here.
# A developer exports their own personal access token, or a project deploy token with the read_package_registry scope.
# A pipeline of THIS repository reads a CI/CD variable of the same name, which somebody has to set first.
# A pipeline's own CI_JOB_TOKEN is not enough: it belongs to this project, and the registry belongs to another one,
# which would have to allowlist this project before that token could read anything.
#
# `min-release-age` is deliberately absent. The sibling webui/.npmrc sets it to 7, and copying that here would hide
# a package published today, which is exactly the package this directory installs.
@simplito:registry=https://gitlab2.simplito.com/api/v4/projects/529/packages/npm/
//gitlab2.simplito.com/api/v4/projects/529/packages/npm/:_authToken=${GITLAB_NPM_TOKEN}
